046 - Abide With Me, 'Tis Eventide
 / 
Key: D
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 46
Topic: Worship - 

Verse 1:
[D]Abide with me, 'tis eventide!
[A]The [A7]day is [G/B]past [A7/C#]and [D]gone;
[D]The shadows of the evening [A]fall;
[G/B]The night [A7]is coming [D]on!
[D]Within [G]my heart a welcome [D]guest,
[D]Within [A/E]my [E7]home abide;

Refrain:
[A]O [A7]Savior, stay this [G/D]night [D]with me;
[D]Behold, [A]'tis [G/B]eventide!
[A/C#]O [Bm]Savior, [G]stay this [D]night with me;
[G]Behold, [Em]'tis [F#m/A]eventide.

Verse 2:
[D]Abide with me, 'tis eventide!
[A]Thy [A7]walk today with [D]me
[D]Has made my heart within [A]me burn,
[G/B]As I [A7]communed with [D]Thee.
[D]Thy [G]earnest words have filled [D]my soul
[D]And [A/E]kept me [E7]near Thy [A]side;

Verse 3:
[D]Abide with me, 'tis eventide!
[A]And [A7]lone will [G/B]be [A7/C#]the [D]night,
[D]If I cannot commune [A]with Thee,
[G/B]Nor find [A7]in Thee my [D]light.
[D]The [G]darkness of the world, [D]I fear,
[D]Would [A/E]in my [E7]home abide;
